==**The four costs map directly onto the lines of every credit-policy statement, and seeing that saves a great deal of time:**
**Cost (i)** → the **opportunity cost of investment in receivables** line;
**Cost (ii)** → the **administration cost** line (and the figure a factor saves);
**Cost (iii)** → the **collection expenses** line;
**Cost (iv)** → the **bad debts** line.
==**A credit-policy numerical is the four costs of §16 arranged in a column against the contribution from additional sales.**==
